                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/pulls/comments/3989306436"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "If we allow the directory to exist, there is no reason to check _if_ it exists upfront, because that is the pretty much first thing that `os.makedirs()` will do.\n```suggestion\n        # Make sure the cache directory exists (and allow for concurrent creation).\n        os.makedirs(self.path, exist_ok=True)\n```",
            "commit_id": "537f1b4117d499d153456d0d92d11f2c76bd7548",
            "created_at": "2026-09-11T12:54:44Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -93,7 +93,8 @@ def __init__(self, path, cache_size=None):\n             self.path = path\n         self.cache_size = cache_size if cache_size is not None else MAX_CACHE_SIZE\n         if not os.path.exists(self.path):\n-            os.makedirs(self.path)\n+            # Guard against multiple processes racing to make the cache.\n+            os.makedirs(self.path, exist_ok=True)",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/cython/cython/pull/7986#discussion_r3989306436",
            "id": 3989306436,
            "line": null,
